## Ported, and altered

`src/net/b12n/raylib_ios/scenes/hello.cljc`, the one scene here, is a port of
raylib-jolt-demo's `core` demo (originally raylib-jlt's), which is raylib's
`core_basic_window`.
It is an altered version: the loop is inverted so the host owns it, geometry
derives from the live screen instead of a fixed 800x450, and drawing moves to
the caller. Its docstring names its original, as the zlib licence's "altered
source versions must be plainly marked as such" asks. The other scenes moved to
raylib-ios-demo, and its NOTICE records their licences.

Some files outside the scenes are derived too. `src/net/b12n/raylib_ios/texture.clj` lifts
the rlgl declarations, the wrap and filter setters, the upload loop and the quad
from raylib-jlt's `lib/src/net/b12n/raylib/textures.clj`, along with the
render-texture, with-render-texture and restore-screen-projection! bodies behind
`target!` and `with-target!`, and adds the id
table, the retained staging buffers, the power-of-two rule and `triangles!`.
That source was added to raylib-jlt on 2026-09-19, after its 2026-09-05
relicence, so it is EPL 2.0 (Copyright (c) 2026 Burin Choomnuan), not the zlib
licence of the block below, which describes the older sources. The scenes that
use it have the same split, and raylib-ios-demo's NOTICE has it. The raylib
C examples behind them are zlib, so their altered-source marking stands.
`src/net/b12n/raylib_ios/texel.cljc` follows the `ImageDraw*` loops of raylib 6.0's
`rtextures.c`, and its tests are worked by hand from them.
`host/draw-circle-gradient` follows `DrawCircleGradient` in raylib 6.0's
`rshapes.c`, and `perlin-grey` in `src/net/b12n/raylib_ios/perlin.cljc` follows
`GenImagePerlinNoise` in `rtextures.c`. raylib's notice is under "Linked". Each
file names its source in its own docstring.

