### What that leaves

Nothing blocking. EPL 2.0 in `LICENSE` covers this project's own work, MIT
covers what came from the demo, from jasalt and from stb_perlin, zlib covers what came from
raylib-jlt, and every one of those notices is in this file. The scenes' own
sources, and the babashka/ffi notice that goes with three of them, are in
raylib-ios-demo's NOTICE.

The four files were also substantially rewritten on 2026-09-04, from the
upstream APIs and this project's own device measurements, taking the expressive
overlap from 207 lines to 119. That work was begun while the licence question
was open and is kept because it made the code better, not because it is needed
any more. What remains in common is interface rather than expression: SDL's
`SDL_SysWMinfo` offsets, raylib's colour values, the Objective-C path to
`safeAreaInsets`, and the order the init calls must happen in. Writing those
differently would make them wrong.

